docs {
  # TPSArena

  Every HTTP endpoint of the backend, in an order that works as a scenario: run the whole
  collection (Runner, or `npx @usebruno/cli run --env Local` in this folder) against the full
  stack (`docker compose up -d --build` at the repository root).

  - Two fresh players (Alice and Bob) are created each run; verification and reset codes are
    read from Mailpit. Requests save ids and tokens in runtime variables for the next ones.
  - Player routes go through the BFF (the game client's only entry point). Game server routes
    and Social's allocation call the Server List directly; health and JWKS use the dev ports.
  - The WebSocket (`ws://localhost:8005/ws`) isn't covered: see services/realtime/PROTOCOL.md.
  - Auth limits verification attempts to 10 per IP per 15 minutes: after several runs in a row,
    wait or clear `auth:ratelimit:verify_*` in the dev Redis.
}
